<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="044" project="messaging-communication-app-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Configure Dataverse Search to index sprk_communication (security-trimmed)</title>
    <phase>5 Release-gated must-haves</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Environment/org search configuration; no application code. Deterministic config task.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Config-only; follows the Dataverse Search enablement recipe.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>deploy, dataverse, config</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Deliver FR-23: configure Dataverse Search so sprk_communication is indexed on subject/body/from/to and findable via the global search bar, security-trimmed. External dependency: Dataverse Search must be enabled for the org and sprk_communication added to the org search config.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Make a keyword search in the Dataverse global search bar return matching sprk_communication records (matching on subject/body/from/to), with results security-trimmed so a user without access to a communication does not see it.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-23 requires global keyword search over communications. External dependency (spec §Dependencies): Dataverse Search enabled + sprk_communication added to the org search config. Dataverse Search is inherently security-trimmed (respects the user's access), which satisfies the NFR-01 non-disclosure requirement for search results.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>Dataverse Search enabled for the target org (external). sprk_communication table present (R1/R2 schema).</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec-FR-23">Index sprk_communication on subject/body/from/to; findable via the global search bar.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">Results MUST be security-trimmed — a user without access to a communication MUST NOT see it in search results.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec-external-dep">Dataverse Search must be enabled at the org level; if it is not, this is an external prerequisite — surface it, do not attempt a workaround indexer.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_communication.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="dataverse-search-config" location="Power Platform admin — search settings + searchable fields">Enable org Dataverse Search; add sprk_communication to the searchable tables; select subject/body/from/to as searchable columns; publish.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Confirm Dataverse Search is enabled for the target org. If not enabled, STOP and surface the external prerequisite (do not build an alternate indexer).</step>
    <step order="2">Add sprk_communication to the org Dataverse Search configuration (searchable tables).</step>
    <step order="3">Select the searchable columns: subject, body, from, to (map to the actual sprk_ logical names). Publish the search configuration.</step>
    <step order="4">Wait for indexing, then verify: a keyword from a communication's subject/body/from/to returns that record via the global search bar.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify security-trimming: as a user WITHOUT access to a communication, the same keyword does NOT return that record.</step>
    <step order="6">Record the enabled columns + verification results in projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/. Update TASK-INDEX.md 044 to complete; document deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If Dataverse Search is not enabled at the org level (a tenant/admin prerequisite), STOP and escalate the external dependency rather than attempting a bespoke search implementation.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>Read, PowerShell, Bash, Skill(task-execute)</tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="config">sprk_communication added to org Dataverse Search config (subject/body/from/to searchable)</output>
    <output type="note">projects/messaging-communication-app-r3/notes/ — enabled columns + verification results</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">sprk_communication is present in the org Dataverse Search configuration with subject/body/from/to as searchable columns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A keyword matching a communication's subject/body/from/to returns that record via the global search bar.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE (security-trimmed): a user without access to a communication does NOT see it in search results for the same keyword.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If Dataverse Search was not enabled, the external prerequisite is surfaced/escalated rather than worked around.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Config-only (not BFF): no publish-size gate. Reference spec FR-23 + external dependency note. Dataverse Search is natively security-trimmed — verify it, do not add trimming logic.</notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill><protocol>Load knowledge first; follow task-execute.</protocol></execution>
</task>
